# Astrodynamics

Course project for **Astrodynamics**, focused on applying orbital mechanics and numerical methods through Python.

## Course

**Astrodynamics**

The course covers the fundamentals of orbital mechanics, including the mathematical and computational methods used to model and analyze spacecraft trajectories.

## Project

The `SOL_Python` directory contains the main Python project developed for the course.

```text
Astrodynamics/
├── SOL_Python/
│   ├── ...
│   └── ...
├── README.md
├── requirements.txt
└── .gitignore
```

The project uses Python to implement and explore astrodynamics concepts through numerical calculations and simulations.

## Topics

* Orbital mechanics
* Keplerian orbits
* Two-body problem
* Orbital propagation
* Numerical methods
* Spacecraft trajectories
* Python-based simulations

## Technologies

* Python
* NumPy
* SciPy
* Matplotlib

## Project status

Coursework in progress.
